---
servings: 2
---
Preheat the oven to 200°C.

Slice the @halloumi{200%g}, @avocado{0.5}, and @cucumber{1}. Roughly chop the @pistachios{2%tbsp}. Finely chop a small handful each of @fresh mint{} and @parsley{}.

Cook the @pearl couscous{0.5%cup} according to package instructions. Drain and set aside.

Toss the @chickpeas{400%g} with 1 tsp olive oil, salt, pepper, @garlic powder{1%tsp} and @hot honey{1%tsp}. Spread on a baking tray and roast for ~{20%minutes}, or until golden and crispy.

Heat 1 tbsp of olive oil and @hot honey{2%tsp} in a non-stick pan over medium heat. Add the halloumi slices and cook ~{1.5%minutes} per side until golden and slightly crispy.

Whisk together the juice of @lemon{0.5}, 3 tbsp olive oil, salt, pepper, mint and parsley.

Divide the couscous between two bowls. Top with @baby spinach{1%cup}, avocado, cucumber, @pickled onions{0.25%cup}, @pomegranate seeds{0.25%cup}, halloumi, pistachios and crispy chickpeas.

Drizzle with the lemon-olive oil dressing and a little extra @hot honey{}.
